WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.020
Join many small molecules end to end,
and you get a polymer: one long chain.

2
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:10.120
Join ethene molecules, and the
polymer is the only product.

3
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.520
Every atom ends up in the chain.

4
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:18.880
But make a polyester, from a diol and a
dicarboxylic acid, and water forms as well.

5
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.460
Where does that water come from, when
some polymers lose no atoms at all?

6
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.740
In this mission, you'll build
polyesters and polyamides,

7
00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.260
and draw the repeat unit of each chain.

8
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:34.520
Then you'll work backwards, from a finished
chain to the monomers that made it.

9
00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.220
Your mission: explain why making
a polyester gives off water,

10
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:41.170
when some plastics lose no atoms at all. 